text:
Maya Chen: quick ping — running into a weird bundling mismatch when using the Node TS SDK in a Next edge function. works locally in dev but fails in prod with a cryptic runtime error. anyone seen this?
Adrian Park: what does the error look like? stack or message pls
Maya Chen: ESM/CJS mismatch at runtime: 'Cannot use import statement outside a module' even though package.json has "type": "module". Next edge build output strips our import to a require and then edge runtime chokes.
Samir Patel: ah yep. common gotcha: next serverless/edge builds can transpile node_modules; sometimes your package's "exports" map or main/module fields confuse the bundler. are you using a published bundle or local path?
Maya Chen: published. package.json has both cjs and esm entries. example usage in our edge handler: ```js
import Redwood from 'redwood-inference'
export default async (req) => {
  const r = await Redwood.generate({ prompt: 'hi' })
  return new Response(r.text)
}
```
Kevin O'Neill: two quick checks: 1) make sure your package.json exports align (./package.json: {"exports":{"import":"./dist/esm/index.js","require":"./dist/cjs/index.js"}}) and 2) for Next edge, ensure the runtime can resolve the ESM entry — sometimes next treats node_modules as CJS and rewrites imports.
Brianna Lopez: for Vite you can set ssr.noExternal: ['redwood-inference'] so it gets bundled into the app's ESM graph. for Next, try transpilePackages: ['redwood-inference'] in next.config.js.
Maya Chen: good call — I tried transpilePackages and the error changed to a streaming issue: in edge runtime streaming responses are not arriving until the connection closes. dev mode streams fine.
Samir Patel: streaming in edge is very sensitive to how you export ReadableStreams. If your SDK wraps native streams with a polyfill at build time it can get lost. are you using any global polyfills like globalThis.ReadableStream?
Maya Chen: we do a tiny wrapper to normalize Node and browser streams. snippet: ```js
// dist/esm/stream-adapter.js
export function toWebReadable(nodeStream) {
  // uses stream.Readable.toWeb in Node 18
}
``` Kevin O'Neill: if Next/Vercel targets edge, Node builtins aren't available. ensure your bundle contains a pure-web implementation. Also avoid conditional requires like `if (!globalThis.ReadableStream) require('stream').Readable` because bundlers will inline that and break the edge build.
Adrian Park: another auth gotcha: building the key into the bundle. If you reference process.env at build time (like const key = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY) Vite/Next might inline it at build step and the edge runtime won't pick up the runtime secret. use runtime env access: `const key = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY` inside the handler and mark it as server-side only.
Maya Chen: thanks — our SDK exposes a helper that reads process.env on import which likely triggered inlining. I'll move env read into a lazy getter.
Brianna Lopez: FYI here's a minimal next.config.js patch that fixed our issues earlier: ```js
// next.config.js
const { withTM } = require('next-transpile-modules')(['redwood-inference'])
module.exports = withTM({
  experimental: { runtime: 'edge' }
})
```
Samir Patel: for Vite/node-edge, vite.config.ts: ```ts
export default defineConfig({
  ssr: { noExternal: ['redwood-inference'] }
})
```
Maya Chen: I pushed a test PR with the lazy env fix and added a tiny web-only stream adapter. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/412 (heading: edge: lazy env + web streams). can someone glance? :eyes:
Adrian Park: looking now. also add a small e2e that runs the edge handler via a local esbuild-based runner so we catch bundler issues in CI.
ci-bot: CI started for pr/412 — build, unit, and edge-smoke tests queued.
Kevin O'Neill: FYI if you need a quick repro, create a tiny Next edge route importing the published package and add `console.log(typeof ReadableStream)` at runtime — it'll show if the runtime used web streams.
Brianna Lopez: reviewed + left one comment about package.json exports ordering. small nit. :+1:
Samir Patel: LGTM once CI green. added an integration step to run Vite SSR bundle in node:18 to catch common transforms.
Maya Chen: thanks all — CI is green 🎉. merging now and will monitor the prod edge deploy. closing this thread after deploy verification.
ci-bot: pr/412 merged by Maya Chen — deployment triggered to staging.
